00:31:27,641 --> 00:31:30,238
where we’d execute on all three of the trade patterns.

564
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:33,624
我喜欢这个交易策略的原因是因为我职业早期犯过的一个错误可能你们大多数也犯过：读到某些东西—比如加拿大的通胀报告，或者央行报告可能你读过《金融时报》或《华尔街日报》然后你意识到：哦，这是重大数据，是游戏改变者
Now, the reason I love this trade strategy is because

565
00:31:33,624 --> 00:31:37,779
one of the mistakes I made very early in my career and probably most of you make

566
00:31:37,779 --> 00:31:41,934
is you read something— whether it’s the inflation report from Canada, maybe a central bank report,

567
00:31:41,934 --> 00:31:46,089
You may have read the Financial Times or the Wall Street Journal and what you recognize is:

568
00:31:46,089 --> 00:31:48,777
Oh, this is really big data, this is a game changer.

575
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:54,730
但实际上，你这样做只是在强化读过的某种偏见
When in fact, what you’re doing there is

576
00:31:54,730 --> 00:31:57,196
you’re simply enforcing a bias from something you might have read.

577
00:31:57,197 --> 00:31:59,458
是在基于所读内容强化自身理解
You’re enforcing your understanding based on something you’ve read.

578
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:09,795
现在，在讲执行方法前先看几个关键原则
Now, before we look at the execution methodology, let’s go over one or two other principles to understand:

580
00:32:11,940 --> 00:32:22,320
首先，这些事件中市场流动性差
First and foremost, when we have these events, there are illiquid markets. Liquidity becomes a premium,

582
00:32:23,160 --> 00:32:27,340
流动性变得稀缺，参与者退出市场
participants disappear from the market. Why take on risk when there’s potential for the unknown?

584
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:31,210
波动性上升的第二个原因：价格移动时价格上下波动——记得之前说的——会吸引越来越多参与者
The second reason volatility arises is that

585
00:32:31,210 --> 00:32:36,467
as price shifts, as price moves up and down—remember, as we said—

586
00:32:36,467 --> 00:32:39,297
it brings in more and more participants.

587
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:43,990
所以价格移动的动态会带来更多参与者
So, the dynamic of price shifting brings in more participants.

588
00:32:43,990 --> 00:32:47,133
话说回来，我之前提过
That said, as I’ve mentioned before,

589
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:56,580
波动性会引发更多波动性
Volatility leads to more volatility.

590
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:03,240
另一个原因：不确定性——这才是关键——
Another reason: uncertainty—this is the real key—

591
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:10,900
不确定性让人们对价格不再敏感
uncertainty means people become less price-sensitive.

592
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:15,131
当市场面临未知事件或担忧时人们不再考虑风险收益只会想：‘我对价格不敏感’‘我只想清仓了结’
So, when there’s an unknown event or something the market is concerned about,

593
00:33:15,131 --> 00:33:17,537
people don’t think in terms of risk-reward,

594
00:33:17,537 --> 00:33:21,748
they don’t think in terms of anything other than, ‘I’m not price-sensitive;

595
00:33:21,748 --> 00:33:24,756
I need to just get out and clear my book.’

596
00:33:24,760 --> 00:33:30,040
这一点很重要，因为这些是风险事件交易的底层规则
And that’s important to understand because, again, these are the underlying rules and principles that govern risk-event trading.

598
00:33:30,620 --> 00:33:34,020
市场会流动性不足
The markets will be illiquid.

599
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:38,100
价格移动会吸引更多参与者
As prices shift, it’s going to bring in more and more participants. Different strategies, different players,

601
00:33:38,760 --> 00:33:40,280
不同策略、不同玩家
exhaustion high, exhaustion low, trend, trend.

602
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,760
会带来更多波动，因为波动自生波动
It’ll bring more volatility because volatility breeds volatility.

603
00:33:44,460 --> 00:33:47,460
不确定性显然让人们对价格不敏感
And obviously, uncertainty means people are price-insensitive.

604
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:51,460
所以别逆某些风险事件而为
So you don’t want to be fading certain risk events.

605
00:33:51,780 --> 00:34:01,926
现在，显然，我给你的风险事件交易关键建议其实很简单
Now, obviously, note that one of the key tips I can give you for risk event trading is very simple.

